<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Auto Reliability Intelligence" description="How Auto Reliability Intelligence handles data, cookies, advertising, and privacy choices.">
  <article><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="updated">Effective date: September 22, 2026</p>
    <h2>Information we collect</h2><p>We collect limited technical information that browsers normally send, such as device type, browser version, referral page, approximate location derived from IP address, and interactions with our pages. If you contact us, we use the information you provide to respond to your request and maintain editorial records.</p>
    <h2>Advertising, cookies, and web beacons</h2><p>We may use Google AdSense and other third-party advertising providers to serve advertisements. These providers may use cookies, web beacons, and similar technologies to measure advertising performance, limit repeat ads, prevent fraud, and show ads that may be relevant to your interests.</p><p>Google and its partners may use the DoubleClick DART cookie to serve ads based on a visitor’s activity on this site and other sites. You can manage ad personalization through <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google’s My Ad Center</a>. You may also opt out of many interest-based advertising practices through <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.</p>
  <h2>How we use information</h2><p>We use information to operate, secure, improve, and measure this website; investigate technical issues; respond to communications; and comply with legal obligations. We do not sell personal information for money.</p>
  <h2>Analytics</h2><p>When enabled, we use Plausible Analytics to understand aggregated website usage, such as which pages are useful and how visitors find the site. Plausible is designed without advertising cookies or cross-site tracking. We use these measurements to improve the service, not to build advertising profiles.</p>
    <h2>GDPR and CCPA/CPRA rights</h2><p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to request access to, correction of, deletion of, or a portable copy of personal information, to object to certain processing, or to limit use of sensitive personal information. California residents may request information about collection, disclosure, and deletion, and may exercise their right to opt out of applicable sharing for cross-context behavioral advertising. EEA and UK residents may also complain to their local supervisory authority.</p><p>To make a privacy request, contact us using the details on our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>. We may need to verify your identity before responding. Authorized agents may submit requests where permitted by law.</p>
    <h2>Data retention and security</h2><p>We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described here, including security, recordkeeping, and legal compliance. We use reasonable administrative and technical safeguards, but no internet transmission or storage system is completely secure.</p>
    <h2>Children and policy updates</h2><p>This site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal information. We may update this policy as our practices or legal requirements change; the effective date above identifies the latest revision.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
